64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Looking at these, Plan B seems the safest! It's mostly paved, so we won't have to worry about the clay slippage or expensive plants. Plus, it's simpler to build than ponds or dense woods!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, your logic is sound regarding the clay. Plan B also respects the tram-commuters' preference for firm ground. However, we must consider the August heat; a paved plaza could become a scorching oven without significant shade.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Plan B is good because it's easy to clean. But Plan D has sports areas, and I saw that volunteers already help with the youth league! Maybe they would be happy to help there?","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, while sports areas are useful, Plan D involves facilities that require constant upkeep. Given the staffing shortage and the failure of previous surface works, Plan B is the most resilient and fiscally responsible choice.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, I agree. Plan B minimizes the high-cost planted areas that drain our budget. While Plan A and C utilize the habitat fund, their long-term maintenance costs would likely overwhelm the city's limited resources.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, you're right about the heat! But Plan B has shade structures. I think it's still better than Plan A, because digging ponds in slippery clay sounds like a nightmare for the builders!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, a fair point. Digging ponds in clay is indeed an invitation to a structural disaster. Plan B is the most rational choice, provided the shade is sufficient to prevent a heat island effect.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Minato,,"I understand. If Plan B is the easiest for the seven workers to look after, then it is a very kind choice. I will agree with everyone if it means the workers don't get too tired.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Minato, that is a thoughtful perspective. Since we have all identified the same risks—labor shortages, soil instability, and rising maintenance costs—Plan B is the only logical choice that ensures long-term stability over short-term beauty.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,I concur. Plan B avoids the financial trap of high-maintenance greenery and the structural risks of the clay. It is the only option that ensures the park remains a sustainable asset rather than a liability.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm really happy we all agree! Plan B is the most realistic and won't cause a huge mess with the clay. It's the best way to make sure the park actually gets finished!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,It is rare that we find such swift consensus. Plan B acknowledges the physical reality of the site and the practical needs of its users without indulging in architectural fantasy. I am satisfied.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I'm happy too. If Plan B is the easiest for the small team to manage, then it's the best choice for everyone. I'll vote for Plan B!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Minako,,I agree. Plan B is the only option that aligns with the evidence of past failures and current budget constraints. It is the most durable and sustainable choice. I will vote for Plan B.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Plan B is the most fiscally responsible option, ensuring we do not burden the city with unsustainable costs. I will also vote for Plan B.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm voting for Plan B too! It's the smartest choice to avoid those clay problems and make sure the park opens on time. Let's do it!,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,My vote is for Plan B. It is the only proposal that respects the ground's temperament and the people's habits without inviting a maintenance catastrophe. Logic and evidence lead us here.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
